 "title": "What Makes a Castle?",
 "cat": "history",
 "emoji": "🏰",
 "sentences": [
  "Not every fortress is a castle.",
  "Scholars define a castle specifically as a private fortified residence for a lord or noble.",
  "Unlike palaces or villas, castles were built primarily for defense.",
  "They appeared in Europe after the Carolingian Empire fell in the 9th and 10th centuries.",
  "Lords used these bases to launch raids and protect their local territory.",
  "Common features included curtain walls, arrowslits, and sturdy portcullises."
